cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nodejs-store in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "nodejs-store: multi-backend data layer for Node.js (MongoDB, MySQL, SQLite, PostgreSQL)"
abstract: >-
  A data layer for Node.js that defines each model once as a pure JSON schema and queries it with
  one MongoDB-style GQL tree dialect across MongoDB, MySQL, SQLite and PostgreSQL. Nested relation
  reads, GROUP BY/HAVING aggregation, computed columns, soft-delete and role-based access control
  are resolved by the shared Rust core rust-store. The Python twin is py-store (PyPI: storepy).
type: software
